            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0726" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9662: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-06T15:00:00+02:00">April 6, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 7—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1302. The various documents issued by the Foreign Office today avoid any
                    statement in the nature of declaration of war against Greece <pb facs="0727"
                        n="715" xml:id="pg715"/> with the exception of the concluding sentence of a
                    memorandum which was attached to the note handed the Greek Minister<anchor
                        n="99" xml:id="d700-f1"/> today. The memorandum concludes with this
                    statement. “The Reich Government can no longer close their eyes to the fact that
                    Greece is making common cause with Britain and must therefore be regarded as
                    Germany’s enemy in the present war with all the consequences that this
                    entails.”</p>
                <p>The text of the note to the Greek Minister has not yet been made public. I have
                    an appointment with the Greek Minister this afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
